                <pb facs="0528" n="448" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg448"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. White.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-02-15"><hi rendition="#italic">February 15,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1299.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your No. 1836, of the 27th ultimo, has been
                    received.</p>
                <p>It rests on Mr. Schabsel Reif to explain satisfactorily his delay in carrying out
                    his declared intention to return to the United States and to show the reasonable
                    certainty of his present declaration to return.</p>
                <p>Until this is done your course in withholding a passport from him is
                    approved.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
